# Gitignored files copied into a new worktree. `.gitignore` syntax; only files that match
# AND are gitignored are copied, so tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# ⚠ ONE FILE, TWO TOOLS — this is not Claude-Code-specific. Claude Code reads it for
# `--worktree` and subagent `isolation: worktree`; worktrunk's `wt step copy-ignored` reads
# the same file with the same semantics. Do not add a second mechanism for either.
#
# ⚠ IT IS ALSO A SAFETY RAIL FOR WORKTRUNK, not just a convenience. `wt step copy-ignored`
# copies **all** gitignored files when this file is absent — which here would mean
# `.filler-smoke/` (15GB) and every `node_modules/`. On btrfs those are reflinks and nearly
# free, but on any other filesystem it is a real copy. Listing files here caps it.
#
# ⚠ WITHOUT THIS, A WORKTREE HAS NO CREDENTIALS. `.env` is gitignored, so a fresh checkout
# never carries it, and everything touching the live stack fails there in a way that reads
# as a code bug rather than missing config. `loomarr-msw` has been in exactly that state.
#
# ⚠ Deliberately NOT listing `*.db`. `DATABASE_URL` is a RELATIVE sqlite path, so each
# worktree gets its own database from its own `.env` — which is the isolation you want.
# Copying the dev databases would give two worktrees the same starting state and, worse,
# invite someone to point them at one file (see the WAL-corruption warnings elsewhere).
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS IGNORED IF A `WorktreeCreate` HOOK IS EVER ADDED. A hook replaces the
# default git behaviour wholesale, and `.worktreeinclude` is not processed in that case —
# the hook would have to copy these files itself. That is a real trap: the hook works, the
# worktree appears, and the credentials are silently absent. Prefer this file; if a hook
# ever becomes necessary, move the copying into it and delete this, rather than leaving
# both and assuming they cooperate.
.env
.phase0.env
